            <pb/>
            <div type="div2">
               <head>A Thanksgiving Dream</head>
               <div type="div3">
                  <head>CHARACTERS</head>
                  <p rend="justify">Jack—A small boy.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">Pilgrim Maids—Five girls in colonial costume.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">Indians—Two boys in Indian costume.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">Pumpkins—Any number small boys and girls having huge paper pumpkins pinned on them.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">Turkeys—Five children with paper turkeys pinned on them.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">Goblins—Any number of small boys wearing hideous false faces.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">After each group has spoken it goes off stage. After Jack’s last speech he leaves stage and all the others return and sing the closing song.</p>
                  <p rend="justify">If desired the costuming may be elaborate, but it is not at all necessary.</p>
                  <lg>
